It's really not bad to play without the numeric pad once you
get used to it. I started playing before the numeric pad was
part of the standard keyboard so I never took the trouble to
learn how to play with it. I assure you, you can do
everything without the num pad that you can do with it and
at least one thing is easier. The commands are in the
Guidebook.

The hjkl orthoganal moves take a little practice. With the
fingers of your right hand on those keys, h and l are easy
since that's the way you want to go. j and k must be
memorized as down and up. The diagonals are all done with
the index finger and they are also intuitive. There are
various modes that involve prefacing the move command with
another keystroke.
